Feature Name:
TelescopeON Command Orchestration

Objective:
Implement distributed TelescopeON command orchestration using TANGO Controls.

System Components:
- CentralNode
- CSPMaster
- SDPMaster

Functional Requirements:
- TelescopeON command is invoked on CentralNode
- CentralNode invokes TelescopeON on CSPMaster and SDPMaster using TANGO DeviceProxy
- CentralNode waits for command completion from all downstream devices
- Each device exposes a CommandStatus attribute for tracking command execution state
- TelescopeON completes successfully only if all devices return ResultCode.OK
- TelescopeON returns FAILED if:
  - any downstream device returns failure
  - timeout occurs
  - exception occurs during command execution

Execution Behaviour:
- TelescopeON should return immediate QUEUED response
- Command execution continues asynchronously in background thread/task
- CentralNode continuously monitors downstream CommandStatus attributes
- Aggregate final result based on all device responses

Non-Functional Requirements:
- Add structured logging for command execution flow
- Add exception handling for communication failures
- Add timeout handling for unresponsive devices
- Follow production-style TANGO Python implementation practices
- Use clear separation of orchestration logic and device command handling

Expected Output:
- TANGO device hierarchy
- Command interaction flow
- Sequence orchestration design
- Production-style Python TANGO device implementation
- Error handling strategy
- Timeout and retry strategy